            <ArticleTitle>Isolated unilateral aplasia of submandibular gland: a rare anomaly detected incidentally on computerized tomography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e54-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.tripleo.2010.03.038</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aplasia of the major salivary glands is a very uncommon anomaly, with isolated aplasia of only 1 submandibular gland being even rarer. We report a case of a 60-year-old woman in whom unilateral aplasia of the left submandibular gland was detected incidentally on computerized tomography with no other associated congenital abnormalities.</AbstractText>
